examples.solution_text:
$f(g(x))=\sqrt{49-x^2}$ and $h(g(x))=-\sqrt{49-x^2}$.
Both composites require:
$\begin{aligned}49-x^2&\ge0\\x^2&\le49\\-7\le x&\le7\end{aligned}$
For $x\in[-7,7]$, the radicand takes every value from $0$ to $49$. Its square root therefore takes every value from $0$ to $7$.
For $f(g(x))$: domain $[-7,7]$, range $[0,7]$.
For $h(g(x))$: domain $[-7,7]$, range $[-7,0]$.
The composite graphs show the included endpoints and maximum or minimum.
